Replace `src/core.mjs` with:
```js
export function solve(s) {
  return new Set(s).size;
}
```

String iteration yields Unicode code points rather than individual UTF-16 code units, so surrogate pairs remain together. The set therefore contains exactly the distinct code points: `solve("😀")` returns `1`, and empty input returns `0`. Use the existing synchronous API unchanged; no dependencies or test edits are needed.

